{"tool_name":"imetagene","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"imetagene","home":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/Imetagene.html","license":"Artistic-2.0","summary":"This package provide a graphical user interface to the metagene package. This will allow people with minimal R experience to easily complete metagene analysis.","addition_date":"2017-01-17T14:57:35Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:54Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["1.4.0"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:imetagene","credit":[{"email":"audrey.lemacon.1@ulaval.ca","name":"Audrey Lemacon","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/Imetagene.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0863"},"format":[{"term":"BAM","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2572"},{"term":"BED","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3003"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2945"},{"term":"Design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2430"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Matrix","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2082"},"format":[{"term":"PDF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3508"},{"term":"PNG","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3603"}]},{"data":{"term":"Plot","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2884"},"format":[{"term":"PDF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3508"},{"term":"PNG","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3603"}]}]}],"name":"Imetagene","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"bioconductor_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pcbi.1004751","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2016 Joly Beauparlant et al.ChIP-Sequencing (ChIP-Seq) provides a vast amount of information regarding the localization of proteins across the genome. The aggregation of ChIP-Seq enrichment signal in a metagene plot is an approach commonly used to summarize data complexity and to obtain a high level visual representation of the general occupancy pattern of a protein. Here we present the R package metagene, the graphical interface Imetagene and the companion package similaRpeak. Together, they provide a framework to integrate, summarize and compare the ChIP-Seq enrichment signal from complex experimental designs. Those packages identify and quantify similarities or dissimilarities in patterns between large numbers of ChIP-Seq profiles. We used metagene to investigate the differential occupancy of regulatory factors at noncoding regulatory regions (promoters and enhancers) in relation to transcriptional activity in GM12878 B-lymphocytes. The relationships between occupancy patterns and transcriptional activity suggest two different mechanisms of action for transcriptional control: i) a \u201cgradient effect\u201d where the regulatory factor occupancy levels follow transcription and ii) a \u201cthreshold effect\u201d where the regulatory factor occupancy levels max out prior to reaching maximal transcription. metagene, Imetagene and similaRpeak are implemented in R under the Artistic license 2.0 and are available on Bioconductor.","authors":[{"name":"Belleau P."},{"name":"Bilodeau S."},{"name":"Deschenes A."},{"name":"Droit A."},{"name":"Joly Beauparlant C."},{"name":"Lamaze F.C."},{"name":"Lemacon A."},{"name":"Samb R."}],"citationCount":7,"date":"2016-08-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"PLoS Computational Biology","title":"metagene Profiles Analyses Reveal Regulatory Element\u2019s Factor-Specific Recruitment Patterns"},"type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Experimental design and studies","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3678"},{"term":"Genetics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3053"},{"term":"Sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Imetagene","home":"https://bio.tools/imetagene","license":"Artistic-2.0","version":"1.4.0","summary":"This package provide a graphical user interface to the metagene package. This will allow people with minimal R experience to easily complete metagene analysis.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:imetagene:1.4.0/cmd/bioconductor.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"manual":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":11,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2017"},{"count":1,"year":"2019"},{"count":1,"year":"2020"},{"count":1,"year":"2021"},{"count":2,"year":"2023"},{"count":2,"year":"2024"},{"count":3,"year":"2016"}],"doi":"10.1371/journal.pcbi.1004751","pmcid":"PMC4990179","pmid":"27538250","ref_count":34,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"1998"},{"count":1,"year":"2002"},{"count":1,"year":"2003"},{"count":1,"year":"2005"},{"count":1,"year":"2006"},{"count":1,"year":"2007"},{"count":1,"year":"2008"},{"count":1,"year":"2009"},{"count":2,"year":"2013"},{"count":3,"year":"2011"},{"count":3,"year":"2014"},{"count":5,"year":"2010"},{"count":5,"year":"2012"},{"count":8,"year":"2015"}],"title":"metagene Profiles Analyses Reveal Regulatory Element's Factor-Specific Recruitment Patterns.","year":2016}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":404,"redirects":[{"status":301,"url":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/Imetagene.html"}],"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}},"support":{"email":true}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:imetagene:1.4.0/lib/bioconductor.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"s